<title>CANADA: Quebec increases minimum wage to C$6.80/hour.</title>
<headline>Quebec increases minimum wage to C$6.80/hour.</headline>
<dateline>QUEBEC CITY 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quebec said on Thursday it will increase the province's minimum wage by C$0.10 an hour to C$6.80 as of October 1, 1997.</p>
<p>Quebec Labour Minister Matthias Rioux said the new wage will aply to about 180,000 workers, mainly in service industries. This represent 6.5 percent of Quebec's workforce.</p>
<p>The minimum wage for employees earning tips will also rise by C$0.10 to C$6.05 an hour.</p>
<p>&quot;These increases, approved by the cabinet, take into account the overall economic indicators, the inflation and the average wages in Quebec,&quot; said Rioux in a statement.</p>
<p>((Reuters Quebec City Bureau: 418-648-6442))</p>
</text>
